[TEXT] The ping from pc4 confirms: **ICMP times out** (no reply, not ICMP unreachable). And crucially, `systemctl status frr` on router6 shows `inactive (dead)` — but FRR is still running from the startup script. More importantly, the iptables rules have 0 packets because the counter check ran before the ping, but the timeout confirms traffic IS being dropped.

Now let me check whether any iptables DROP counter has incremented after the ping and also verify if the protocol-0 catch-all is really matching ICMP:
