[TEXT] **Confirmed!** Rule 4 (`DROP all from eth2`) counted exactly **4 packets, 336 bytes** — precisely the 4 ICMP echo requests from the ping test. The packets DID reach router6 via the correct static-route chain, but were silently dropped by the broad iptables catch-all DROP.

From `iptables -S FORWARD`, the last rule is `-A FORWARD -i eth2 -j DROP` (no `-p` flag = all protocols). This is the fault.

